n zero  multiplied by itself zero times and it  depends what context you're using  sometimes people will say that this is  undefined but many more times at least  in my experience this will be defined to  be one so defined to be e one and the  reason why even though this is  completely non-intuitive and you could  type in zero to the zeroth power in  Google and it'll give you one  the reason even though this is  completely non-intuitive the reason why  this is defined to be this way is that  it makes a lot of formulas work and then  what in particular the binomial formula  works the but for your binomial  coefficients which I'm not going to go  over right here when 0 to the zeroth  power is equal to 1 so that's an  interesting thing for you to think about  what that might even mean so let's talk  about some of the other properties and  then we can we can put them all together  with a couple of example problems I told  you in the last video what it means to  raise to a negative power a to the  negative 1 power  or maybe I should say a to the negative  B power is equal to 1 over a to the B  power so just to do that with a couple  of concrete examples 3 to the negative 3  power is equal to 1 over 3 to the 3rd  power which is equal to 1 over 3 times 3  times 3 which is equal to 1 over 27 if I  were to ask you what if I were to ask  you what one-third one-third let's say  to the negative 2 power is well this is  going to be equal to 1 over one-third to  the second power you get rid of the  negative and you inverse it so this is  going to be equal to 1 over what's  one-third times one-third 1/9 which is  equal to this is 1 divided by 1/9 the  same thing as 1 times 9 so this is equal  to 9 and this makes complete sense  because one-third remember one-third is  the same thing as 3 to the negative 1  power right the 3 to the negative  one is one this is equal to 1 over 3 to  the 1 power which is the same thing as  1/3 so if we replace 1/3 with 3 to the  negative 1 this is 3 